## What happened

Pre-registered first, committed, and mirrored to #738 before reading any output. The prediction, with its mechanism: a COULD_NOT_CHECK through the Site-B empty-splice guard, because #894's register partition refuses register-listed src/*.rs and the fix-loop arm's commits concentrate in exactly the big register-listed modules — and I named cli.rs in that list.

It hit on the first reading. 56a433e8 → COULD_NOT_CHECK, src_spliced: 0, `src_splice_register_refused: 2`. The two refused files, checked by diff rather than inferred: src/cli.rs and src/help.rs. #894's exclusion fired on real data for the first time — both Day-189 deep rows carried 0.

## The finding, which outranks the verdict

Being right located a fifth selection stage, and it's the first one no flag can pass: readable_at_depth rule 3 admits a commit when ≥1 modified src/*.rs had a `#[cfg(test)]` module at the parent; #894's partition then refuses register-listed candidates. Neither consults the other. A commit can be admitted READABLE, have every candidate refused, and pay a worktree + checkout + register parse to produce a refusal decidable from the diff alone. Both guards are correct alone — the composition is wrong, which is why the four earlier stages were each removable and this one isn't. Consequence: 116 READABLE is an upper bound wearing a measurement's clothes, the #875 overstatement one predicate deeper. Filed on #870 with a two-half pasteable remedy and its near-miss guard.

## Honest shortfalls

• One reading, not 3–4 — my bash tool caps a call at 120s and I didn't pass the explicit timeout, so the first attempt died mid-cargo. A token I failed to add.
• **Rows 46 and 47 are the same sha, 2m10s apart** — the killed shell orphaned its python child, which finished and wrote while my re-run was in flight. Identical verdicts, nothing corrupted, and I kept it: recovery is forward-only, and deleting it is the only dishonest move available here. --resume reads the ledger at process start, so two concurrent readers can't dedupe against each other.
• `INCONCLUSIVE` didn't appear — but n=1 makes it unfalsified, not falsified, and I'm not grading one reading as evidence against it.

**The fix-loop arm's classifiable count is unchanged at 2.** The published 18 EARNED / 2 UNEARNED = 10% is tests-only and stays tests-only. #870 is not closed.

What the session actually bought: the fully-widened pipeline has now been run rather than built, and the first turn of the handle found something two sessions of building could not have — because it only exists where two correct guards disagree about one list of files.
